WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.912
RouteWise makes AI inference cheaper while enforcing your reliability requirements.

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:09.462
In our benchmark, it cut inference cost by seventy-seven percent

00:00:09.638 --> 00:00:11.412
compared with grounded Super.

00:00:11.775 --> 00:00:15.238
That’s about eighty dollars instead of three hundred forty-nine per

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.325
million requests.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.500
On the same three hundred twelve synthetic conversations, ninety-eight point

00:00:21.512 --> 00:00:25.638
four percent were completed correctly without review, with zero wrong

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.750
answers released.

00:00:27.112 --> 00:00:30.500
Independent human validation is complete for this dataset.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.562
Not every request needs your most powerful model.

00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:39.462
We benchmark NVIDIA Nemotron models on Nebius Token Factory, using

00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:43.438
the same workload and declared accuracy and latency targets.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.975
Nano handles the easy cases; Super handles requests that fail

00:00:47.988 --> 00:00:48.788
validation.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.712
Tighten the response-time target, and the recommendation switches to Super.

00:00:54.075 --> 00:00:57.612
Ask for more certainty than the data supports, and RouteWise

00:00:57.625 --> 00:00:58.725
recommends nothing.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.050
Reliability also means knowing when to stop.

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:05.812
Here, the recorded route corrects a missing refund date from

00:01:05.825 --> 00:01:07.025
the store’s timestamp.

00:01:07.388 --> 00:01:09.950
An ambiguous date goes to human review.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.575
Here’s a fresh call to Nebius Token Factory.

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:17.300
You can inspect the model’s raw response, the final answer,

00:01:17.538 --> 00:01:19.812
the checks, and the full request cost.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.012
Download the chosen setup, requirements, and evidence.

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:28.925
These savings cover inference usage; hosting and review cost extra.

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:32.712
The dataset is synthetic, and a later noise test missed

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:33.800
its latency target.

00:01:34.162 --> 00:01:38.000
RouteWise makes the savings, tradeoffs, and limits visible.
